less than a week after a deadly crash  the community is coming together to  remember 31-year-old cyclist benjamin  black a ghost ride memorial is being  held tonight to honor him madison  kimbrough joins us live near where the  crash happened near the 215 and north  fifth street and madison people in the  area tell you speeding is a big issue  there  [Music]  sasha resident sharing that this is no  surprise as drivers as you can see right  now go way above the speed limit on  these roads the crash happened in this  newly developed area known as  saddlebrook at thule springs in north  las vegas the street has a speed limit  of 25 miles per hour but unfortunately  that hasn't stopped drivers from racing  up and down and police say speed was a  factor in the crash that took ben  black's life early sunday morning a  woman we spoke to the night of black's  vigil who lives in the neighborhood says  things have gotten out of hand in the  last year and a half  no matter what time of day you come out  in the morning might be like seven or  eight o'clock when my son is literally  having to cross the street to go to his  bus stop there are cars literally flying  through here there's times like ten ten  eleven o'clock at night we can be laying  in a bed and it sounds like literally  people are out here drag racing  neighbors say there has been an ongoing  discussion on the community's facebook  page about how to make sure a tragedy  like this does not happen again many  asking the builder kb home to install  speed bumps or street lights in between  intersections as you can see there are  flowers candles and photos from the  vigil that was held for black earlier  this week and the ghost ride memorial  for him starts at 7 30 tonight it's open  to the public reporting in north las  vegas madison kimbrough live local now
 

